S="Moses"
D("2026-11-16",S,"The Baby in the Basket","a K–2nd grader, with help","Exodus 2:10",[(10,"When the child grew older, she brought him to Pharaoh’s daughter, and he became her son. She named him Moses, “Because,” she said, “I drew him out of the water.”")],
"Moses in the river",[
"Many years after Joseph, Jacob’s family had grown into a huge nation called Israel. A new Pharaoh came who didn’t remember Joseph. He was afraid of the Israelites, so he made them slaves. Then he gave a terrible order: every baby boy born to the Israelites must be thrown into the Nile River.",
"One Israelite mother had a baby boy, and she hid him for three months. When she couldn’t hide him anymore, she made a little basket, covered it with tar so it would float, put her baby inside, and set it among the reeds by the river. His big sister Miriam watched to see what would happen.",
"Pharaoh’s own daughter came down to the river to bathe. She saw the basket and opened it. The baby was crying, and she felt sorry for him. Miriam bravely ran up: “Should I find a Hebrew woman to take care of him for you?” She ran and got the baby’s own mother! The princess named him Moses, and God kept him safe for a big job ahead."],
"God protects",["Pharaoh wanted to destroy God’s people, but God used a basket, a brave big sister, and even Pharaoh’s own daughter to protect baby Moses. Nothing can stop God’s plans."],
["Where did Moses’ mother put him? Who watched over the basket?","How was Miriam brave? Who did she bring to take care of Moses?","Pharaoh’s order was meant to destroy Israel. How did God turn it around?"],
"Lord God, thank You for protecting baby Moses, and for protecting us. Thank You for brave big sisters and brothers.","Help us be brave to help others, like Miriam.",
"Moses’ mother put him in a basket in the river. Pharaoh’s daughter found him, and God kept him safe!",
["Pharaoh made the Israelites [slaves].","Moses’ mother put him in a [basket].","His big sister was [Miriam].","Pharaoh’s [daughter] found the baby.","Moses means “drawn out of the [water].”"],
["MOSES","BASKET","RIVER","MIRIAM","NILE","BABY"],[("Who found the baby in the basket?",["Pharaoh’s daughter","Pharaoh"],0),("Who protected Moses?",["God","Nobody"],0)],
"Draw baby Moses in his basket in the reeds.",("Exodus 2:10","“I drew him out of the water.”"),
scene(waves(276,260,636),basket(400),person(150,beard=False,arms="open",hair="wrap"),person(250,beard=False,arms="mixed",hair="curly",s=.7),sun(560,56),label="Coloring picture: baby Moses in a basket among the reeds"))

D("2026-11-17",S,"The Burning Bush","an older kid","Exodus 3:14",[(14,"God said to Moses, “I AM WHO I AM.” And he said, “Say this to the people of Israel: ‘I AM has sent me to you.’”")],
"God calls Moses",[
"Moses grew up in Pharaoh’s palace, but he knew he was an Israelite. One day he saw an Egyptian beating an Israelite slave, and in anger Moses killed the Egyptian. Pharaoh found out, and Moses ran far away into the desert. For forty years he lived there as a shepherd.",
"One day, while watching his sheep near a mountain, Moses saw something strange: a bush on fire, but it wasn’t burning up! As he walked closer, God called from the bush, “Moses, Moses! Take off your sandals, for the place where you are standing is holy ground.”",
"God said, “I have seen My people suffering in Egypt. I am sending you to Pharaoh to bring them out.” Moses was scared. “Who am I to do that? And what’s Your name, if they ask?” God answered, “I AM WHO I AM.” God always was, always is, and always will be. Moses still made excuses, but God promised, “I will be with you.”"],
"I AM",["God’s name, “I AM,” means He doesn’t depend on anything. He has no beginning and no end. Later Jesus said, “Before Abraham was, I am,” telling everyone He is God. The great I AM was with Moses, and He is with us."],
["What was strange about the bush? Why did Moses take off his sandals?","What excuses did Moses make? What did God promise him?","Jesus used the name “I am” about Himself (John 8:58). What was He saying?"],
"Holy God, You are the great I AM. Thank You for calling Moses even after his mistakes, and for calling us too.","When we feel too small for what You ask, remind us that You are with us.",
"God spoke to Moses from a bush that burned but didn’t burn up! God’s name is I AM.",
["Moses took care of [sheep] in the desert.","The bush was on [fire] but didn’t burn up.","Moses took off his [sandals].","God’s name is “I [AM].”","God said, “I will be [with] you.”"],
["BUSH","FIRE","HOLY","SANDALS","MOSES","LORD"],[("Did the bush burn up?",["Yes","No"],1),("What did God send Moses to do?",["Free His people","Stay hidden"],0)],
"Draw the burning bush and Moses taking off his sandals.",("Exodus 3:14","“I AM WHO I AM.”"),
scene(mountains(),bush(420),person(220,beard=True,arms="open",hair="wrap"),sheep(560,.7),label="Coloring picture: Moses at the burning bush"))

D("2026-11-18",S,"Let My People Go","a 3rd–5th grader","Exodus 5:1–2",[(1,"Afterward Moses and Aaron went and said to Pharaoh, “Thus says the LORD, the God of Israel, ‘Let my people go, that they may hold a feast to me in the wilderness.’”"),(2,"But Pharaoh said, “Who is the LORD, that I should obey his voice and let Israel go? I do not know the LORD, and moreover, I will not let Israel go.”")],
"The plagues",[
"Moses and his brother Aaron went to Pharaoh with God’s message: “Let My people go!” But Pharaoh laughed. “Who is the Lord? I don’t know Him, and I won’t let Israel go.” Instead, he made the slaves work even harder.",
"So God sent plagues on Egypt. The Nile River turned to blood. Frogs hopped everywhere: in beds, in ovens, in bowls. Then came gnats, flies, sick animals, painful sores, giant hailstorms, and swarms of locusts that ate every green plant. Then thick darkness covered Egypt for three days, but the Israelites had light where they lived.",
"Each time, Pharaoh promised to let the people go. And each time, as soon as the plague stopped, he changed his mind and hardened his heart. Pharaoh found out who the Lord was: the one true God, stronger than all the gods of Egypt. But he still wouldn’t listen."],
"Hard hearts",["Pharaoh kept saying no to God, again and again, until his heart became hard. When God speaks to us through His Word, the best thing we can do is listen right away. A soft heart says, “Yes, Lord.”"],
["What did Moses tell Pharaoh? Name as many plagues as you can.","Why do you think Pharaoh kept changing his mind?","What does it mean to have a hard heart? How does God soften hearts?"],
"Mighty God, You are stronger than every power in the world. Thank You for hearing Your people’s cries.","Give us soft hearts that listen to Your Word and say yes to You.",
"Pharaoh wouldn’t let God’s people go, so God sent plagues. Pharaoh learned who the Lord is!",
["Moses said, “Let my [people] go!”","Moses’ brother was [Aaron].","The Nile turned to [blood].","[Frogs] hopped everywhere.","Pharaoh’s heart was [hard]."],
["PLAGUES","FROGS","LOCUSTS","DARKNESS","AARON","PHARAOH"],[("Did Pharaoh listen the first time?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who is stronger than Egypt’s gods?",["The Lord","Pharaoh"],0)],
"Draw your favorite plague. (Frogs are fun!)",("Exodus 5:1","“Let my people go.”"),
scene(pyramids(),throne(130),crown(130,140),person(130,beard=True,arms="open",hair="wrap",s=.9),person(280,beard=True,arms="up",hair="short"),''.join(f'<ellipse cx="{x}" cy="290" rx="14" ry="9"/><circle cx="{x-6}" cy="282" r="3"/><circle cx="{x+6}" cy="282" r="3"/>' for x in (370,420,600)),label="Coloring picture: Moses before Pharaoh with frogs"))

D("2026-11-19",S,"The Passover","an older kid","Exodus 12:13",[(13,"The blood shall be a sign for you, on the houses where you are. And when I see the blood, I will pass over you, and no plague will befall you to destroy you, when I strike the land of Egypt.")],
"The lamb’s blood",[
"God told Moses there would be one last plague, the worst of all: the firstborn son in every house in Egypt would die. But God gave His people a way to be safe. Each family was to take a perfect lamb, sacrifice it, and paint its blood on the doorposts of their house.",
"That night, the families ate the lamb with bread made without yeast, because there was no time for the bread to rise. They ate with their sandals on and their walking sticks in their hands, ready to leave. At midnight, the Lord went through Egypt. But wherever He saw the blood on the door, He passed over that house.",
"A great cry went up in Egypt, even in Pharaoh’s palace. Finally Pharaoh called Moses in the night: “Go! Take your people and go!” After 430 years, Israel walked out of Egypt free. God told them to remember that night every year with a feast called the Passover."],
"Covered by the Lamb",["The blood of the lamb saved God’s people from death. Jesus is our Passover Lamb (1 Corinthians 5:7). His blood covers us, so death passes over us. And on the night before He died, Jesus celebrated the Passover with His disciples and gave us the Lord’s Supper."],
["What did the families paint on their doors? What did God do when He saw it?","Why did they eat with their sandals on and bread with no yeast?","Jesus is called our Passover Lamb. How does Passover help us understand the cross and the Lord’s Supper?"],
"Lord Jesus, You are our Passover Lamb. Thank You for covering us with Your blood so that death passes over us.","Thank You for the Lord’s Supper, where You give us Your body and blood for the forgiveness of sins.",
"God’s people painted lamb’s blood on their doors, and the Lord passed over them. Jesus is our Passover Lamb!",
["Each family took a perfect [lamb].","They painted [blood] on the doorposts.","The Lord [passed] over the houses with blood.","Pharaoh finally said, “[Go]!”","[Jesus] is our Passover Lamb."],
["PASSOVER","LAMB","BLOOD","DOOR","FREE","BREAD"],[("What made the houses safe?",["The lamb’s blood","Locked doors"],0),("Who is our Passover Lamb?",["Jesus","Moses"],0)],
"Draw a house with blood on the doorposts, and a family inside eating.",("Exodus 12:13","“When I see the blood, I will pass over you.”"),
scene(moon(560,56),stars(10,13,(240,640)),house(330),lamb(150),'<path d="M310,300 V240 M350,300 V240 M314,238 H346" fill="none" stroke-width="6"/>',label="Coloring picture: a house with blood on the doorposts and a lamb"))

D("2026-11-20",S,"Through the Sea","a 3rd–5th grader","Exodus 14:13–14",[(13,"And Moses said to the people, “Fear not, stand firm, and see the salvation of the LORD, which he will work for you today. For the Egyptians whom you see today, you shall never see again."),(14,"The LORD will fight for you, and you have only to be silent.”")],
"Crossing the Red Sea",[
"God led His people out of Egypt with a pillar of cloud during the day and a pillar of fire at night. But soon Pharaoh changed his mind again. “What have we done? We let our slaves go!” He chased after them with six hundred chariots.",
"The Israelites were trapped: the sea in front of them and Pharaoh’s army behind them. They panicked. “Did you bring us out here to die?” But Moses said, “Don’t be afraid. Stand still and see how the Lord will save you. The Lord will fight for you.”",
"God told Moses to stretch out his staff over the sea. A strong wind blew all night, and the water split in two, with walls of water on the right and on the left! The people walked through on dry ground. When the Egyptians followed, the water came crashing back. Israel was safe on the other side, and Miriam led everyone in a song of praise."],
"The Lord fights for you",["The people couldn’t save themselves. They could only watch God save them. That’s what salvation is: God does the work. Christians have always seen the Red Sea as a picture of Baptism, where God brings us through water from slavery to freedom."],
["What was in front of the Israelites? What was behind them?","Moses said, “The Lord will fight for you.” What did the people have to do?","How is crossing the Red Sea like Baptism (1 Corinthians 10:1–2)?"],
"Lord God, You fought for Israel at the Red Sea, and You fought for us at the cross. Thank You for saving us when we couldn’t save ourselves.","When we feel trapped, help us stand still and trust You.",
"God split the Red Sea so His people could walk through on dry ground!",
["Pharaoh chased them with [chariots].","Moses stretched out his [staff].","The water made two [walls].","They walked on [dry] ground.","Moses said, “The Lord will [fight] for you.”"],
["SEA","STAFF","CHARIOTS","WIND","DRY","SAVED"],[("Did the people have to fight the Egyptians?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who split the sea?",["God","The wind by itself"],0)],
"Draw the walls of water with God’s people walking through.",("Exodus 14:14","“The LORD will fight for you.”"),
scene('<path d="M4,300 V90 Q120,60 230,90 V300 Z M410,300 V90 Q520,60 636,90 V300 Z"/>'+waves(130,8,226)+waves(200,8,226)+waves(130,414,632)+waves(200,414,632),person(320,beard=True,arms="up",hair="wrap"),'<path d="M352,140 L360,300" fill="none" stroke-width="5"/>',label="Coloring picture: Moses leading the people through the Red Sea"))

D("2026-11-21",S,"Bread from Heaven","a K–2nd grader, with help","John 6:35",[(35,"Jesus said to them, “I am the bread of life; whoever comes to me shall not hunger, and whoever believes in me shall never thirst.")],
"Manna in the desert",[
"After crossing the sea, God’s people traveled into the desert. Soon they were hungry, and they started complaining. “We had plenty of food in Egypt! You brought us here to starve!” They forgot all the amazing things God had just done.",
"But God was patient. He said, “I will rain bread from heaven for you.” The next morning, the ground was covered with little white flakes that tasted like wafers made with honey. The people asked, “What is it?” In Hebrew that is “manna,” and that became its name. God also sent quail for meat in the evening.",
"Every morning, each family gathered just enough for that day. If they tried to save extra, it got wormy and smelly! But on the sixth day, they gathered twice as much, so they could rest on the Sabbath. For forty years in the desert, God fed His people every single day."],
"Daily bread",["God gave manna one day at a time, so the people would learn to trust Him every day. That’s why Jesus taught us to pray, “Give us this day our daily bread.” And Jesus Himself is the true bread from heaven, who gives eternal life."],
["What did God send from heaven? What did the people call it?","Why couldn’t they save extra manna? What was God teaching them?","Jesus said, “I am the bread of life.” What does He mean? How do we “eat” this bread?"],
"Heavenly Father, thank You for feeding Your people in the desert, and for giving us our daily bread. Thank You for Jesus, the bread of life.","When we complain, forgive us, and teach us to trust You day by day.",
"God rained manna from heaven every morning to feed His people. Jesus is the bread of life!",
["The people [complained] in the desert.","God sent bread from [heaven].","They called it [manna].","It tasted like wafers with [honey].","Jesus is the bread of [life]."],
["MANNA","BREAD","QUAIL","DESERT","HONEY","DAILY"],[("Could they save extra manna?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who is the bread of life?",["Jesus","Moses"],0)],
"Draw the ground covered with manna, and people gathering it.",("John 6:35","“I am the bread of life.”"),
scene(mountains(),flakes(50,7),tent(520),person(170,beard=False,arms="mixed",hair="wrap"),person(320,beard=True,arms="open",hair="short",s=.75),bread(380),label="Coloring picture: God’s people gathering manna in the desert"))

D("2026-11-22",S,"The Ten Commandments","Mom or Dad","Exodus 20:2–3",[(2,"“I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery."),(3,"“You shall have no other gods before me.")],
"Mount Sinai",[
"Three months after leaving Egypt, God’s people came to a mountain called Sinai. Thunder rumbled, lightning flashed, and a thick cloud covered the mountain. A trumpet blast grew louder and louder, and the whole mountain shook. The people trembled.",
"God called Moses up the mountain, and there God gave His Ten Commandments, written on two stone tablets by God’s own finger. But notice how God began: “I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of slavery.” God rescued His people first, and then He gave them His commandments.",
"The commandments teach us how to love God (the first three) and how to love our neighbor (the other seven). They show us God’s good will. They also show us our sin, because no one keeps them perfectly. Only Jesus did. He kept every commandment for us, and then died for all the times we break them."],
"Rescued, then commanded",["God doesn’t say, “Obey Me and then I’ll save you.” He says, “I saved you, so now live as My people.” That’s why each explanation in the Small Catechism begins, “We should fear and love God.” We obey out of love for the God who rescued us."],
["Where did God give the Ten Commandments? What were they written on?","What did God say before He gave the commandments? Why does that order matter?","The Law shows us our sin. How does that make us need Jesus? Which commandment is hardest for you?"],
"Holy God, thank You for rescuing us and for giving us Your good commandments. Forgive us for breaking them, and thank You for Jesus, who kept them all for us.","Help us fear, love, and trust You above all things, and love our neighbor.",
"God gave His Ten Commandments on Mount Sinai, written on stone tablets with His own finger!",
["God gave the commandments on Mount [Sinai].","They were written on two stone [tablets].","The first commandment: You shall have no other [gods].","The commandments show us our [sin].","[Jesus] kept them all for us."],
["SINAI","TABLETS","LAW","TEN","THUNDER","LOVE"],[("Did God rescue His people before giving the commandments?",["Yes","No"],0),("Who kept all the commandments perfectly?",["Jesus","Moses"],0)],
"Draw the two stone tablets. Can you write the numbers 1 to 10 on them?",("Exodus 20:3","“You shall have no other gods before me.”"),
scene('<path d="M60,300 L320,60 L580,300 Z"/>',cloud(260,60),cloud(360,80),'<path d="M150,100 L130,140 L146,140 L126,180 L170,128 L154,128 L168,100 Z M480,90 L462,130 L478,130 L458,170 L500,118 L486,118 L498,90 Z"/>',tablets(320,190),person(180,beard=True,arms="up",hair="wrap",s=.7),label="Coloring picture: the Ten Commandments on Mount Sinai"))
